WI-mifag's blocker moved from INV-linub to WI-nanom (pyright/SCIP receiver
typing, ADR-0012 multi-fidelity coexistence). INV-linub is the class for a
catalogued I/O sink reaching its CATALOGUE entry through the F3 gate; gating
methods here needs FIRST-PARTY method resolution in the call graph. Same
capability, different consumer -- closing INV-linub would not have delivered it.

Also records a second blindness this module's own docstring did not state:
widening GATED_KINDS is not sufficient, because collect_production_references
is a standalone ast walk with no analyzer involvement and indexes an
ast.Attribute under its bare node.attr, so set.add and Store.add both land in
refs.loads["add"] however well the call graph is typed.

Docstrings only; no behaviour change.

